---
title: Street Light and Pole Detection — Workflow
---
flowchart TB
  A([User opens the app])
  B[Click a spot or draw a scan area on the map]
  C[Load street photos from Mapillary]
  D[Object detection — AI draws a box around each object]
  E[Estimate where each object sits on the map]
  F[Dashboard — map, labeled photos, counts by class]

  A --> B --> C --> D --> E --> F

  D --- CLASSES["Detection classes<br/>Primary focus: Street Lights and Poles<br/>Also: Traffic Signals, Cars, Trees, Buildings, People, Motorcycles"]

  subgraph LOC["How we estimate object location"]
    L1[Use camera GPS and which way the camera was facing]
    L2[Use where the object appears in the photo left / center / right]
    L3[For poles and street lights: estimate distance from typical height in the image]
    L4[Area scans: same object in several photos — sight lines cross for a better pin]
    L1 --> L2 --> L3 --> L4
  end

  D --> LOC
  LOC --> E
